+# RED-SAYS-WHAT-1 — report the last observed host state
+
+Base: `957ef143a1d1effdd3f6a7f8281ed7ce7f458b9b`.
+
+## What changes
+
+The integration test helper `eventually/2` reduces every observation to a boole
an, so its timeout
+cannot distinguish a host that remained `{:ok, pid}` from any other unexpected
state. A sibling
+helper, `eventually_value/3`, retains the last probe result and returns either
`{:ok, value}` or
+`{:timeout, last_value}` while preserving the existing 300 attempts and 10 ms w
ait per attempt.
+
+Only the assertion in *"a mirror host restart under a live attachment is surviv
ed"* uses the new
+helper. Its timeout now names the last result returned by `Hosts.document/2`. T
he other eight
+`eventually/2` call sites and `eventually/2` itself remain unchanged.
+
+## Arm
+
+The test name is unchanged and is already declared in `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN-NEXT
-P7.md`:
+
+`<!-- ARM: a mirror host restart under a live attachment is survived -->`
+
+No duplicate ARM declaration is added here. The mutation arm removes `DocHost.s
top(old_host)` in a
+throwaway copy and requires the failure to include `last observed: {:ok, #PID<`
 rather than the old
+boolean-only `Expected truthy, got false`.
+
+## Fence
+
+The implementation is test-only: this plan and
+`test/integration/markdown_editor_goal_test.exs`. No production code or other t
est file changes.
